Derived entries (@code{hbar}, @code{eps0}, @code{mu0}, @code{sigma},
@code{R0}, @code{V0}) are stored as formulas over the exact defining
constants and expand on conversion.  The physics calculator family
deliberately does @emph{not} read this table --- it carries its own
private numeric constants so @code{lorentz(0.5)} works without the
units machinery (@pxref{Calculator Families}).
